#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "provisioning.security"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Note Admin Permissions
	Testing to assure that provisioning note admin permissions works properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a provisioning user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | provisioning.admin                    |
	| Email Address | provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Provisioning                          |
	| Last Name     | Admin                                 |
	* I assign the provisioning user with the email address "provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken" to the provisioning role "Provisioning Admin"
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | prm.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRM                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | prm.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRM                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Misper - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| MISPERPERMIS |
	| MISPER       |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| MISPERPERMIS |
	| MISPER       |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from provisioning
	| provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken |

Scenario: Create note
	Testing the ability to create a platinum subcription in Dossiera and adding a general plain note via the provisioning account details page and viewing the note in the provisioning account details page 

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Misper - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRM                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRM                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Permis - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Permis"
	And I click on the account with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I expand the side panel on the account details page
	And I click on the "Notes" side panel tab
	And I create a note with the content "Account Note Content" on the account details page
	Then I should be able to view the "General" type note with the content "Account Note Content" and the following values
	| Author  | Provisioning Admin   |
	| Content | Account Note Content |
	And I should not be able to view the "Pinned" type note with the content "Account Note Content"
	And I should not be able to view the view archived notes link
	When I click on the "History" tab
	And I generate the account ID value for "Permis - ${staticProjectName}"
	Then the history entry with the keyword "Provisioning Admin > Added Note" with the field value "creatorName" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Admin > Added Note |
	| Update Field Name           | creatorName                     |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                             |
	| Update Field New Value      | Provisioning Admin              |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Provisioning Admin > Added Note" with the field value "format" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Admin > Added Note |
	| Update Field Name           | format                          |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                             |
	| Update Field New Value      | Plain                           |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Provisioning Admin > Added Note" with the field value "type" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Admin > Added Note |
	| Update Field Name           | type                            |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                             |
	| Update Field New Value      | General                         |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Provisioning Admin > Added Note" with the field value "priority" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Admin > Added Note |
	| Update Field Name           | priority                        |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                             |
	| Update Field New Value      | 2                               |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Provisioning Admin > Added Note" with the field value "content" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Admin > Added Note |
	| Update Field Name           | content                         |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                             |
	| Update Field New Value      | Account Note Content            |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Provisioning Admin > Added Note" with the field value "accountId" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Admin > Added Note |
	| Update Field Name           | accountId                       |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                             |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticAccountId}              |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Provisioning Admin > Added Note" with the field value "status" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Admin > Added Note |
	| Update Field Name           | status                          |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                             |
	| Update Field New Value      | Approved                        |

Scenario: Update general note
	Testing the ability to create a platinum subcription in Dossiera and adding a general note and updating the note via the provisioning page and viewing the note in the provisioning account details page 

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Misper - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRM                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRM                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Permis - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I create a note for the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Agent Name | Koroneiki User       |
	| Content    | Account Note Content |
	| Format     | Plain                |
	| Priority   | 2                    |
	| Status     | Approved             |
	| Type       | General              |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Permis"
	And I click on the account with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I expand the side panel on the account details page
	And I click on the "Notes" side panel tab
	And I click on the "Edit" button for the "General" note with the content "Account Note Content"
	And I edit a "General" note with the content "Account Note Content" on the account details page to have the new content "Account Note Edited Content"
	Then I should be able to view the "General" type note with the content "Account Note Edited Content" and the following values
	| Author      | Koroneiki User              |
	| Create Date | Edited                      |
	| Content     | Account Note Edited Content |
	And I should not be able to view the "Pinned" type note with the content "Account Note Edited Content"
	And I should not be able to view the "General" type note with the content "Account Note Content"
	And I should not be able to view the "Pinned" type note with the content "Account Note Content"
	And I should not be able to view the view archived notes link
	When I click on the "History" tab
	Then the history entry with the keyword "Provisioning Admin > Updated Note" with the field value "content" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Admin > Updated Note |
	| Update Field Name           | content                           |
	| Update Field Original Value | Account Note Content              |
	| Update Field New Value      | Account Note Edited Content       |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Provisioning Admin > Updated Note" with the field value "modifierName" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Admin > Updated Note |
	| Update Field Name           | modifierName                      |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                               |
	| Update Field New Value      | Provisioning Admin                |

